# Gitignored files copied into every new Claude Code worktree.
#
# A worktree is a checkout of *tracked* files, so a fresh one has no env file
# and `commands.dev` cannot start in it — which makes the evidence gate
# (docs/workflow/review-policy.md) unsatisfiable. Claude Code reads this file at
# worktree creation and copies the matching paths in from the main repo.
#
# Gitignore syntax, one pattern per line. Only paths that are actually
# gitignored *and* present in the main checkout can match, so a pattern for a
# file you don't have is simply a no-op — and no tracked file can be pulled in
# by mistake.
#
# Applies to the `claude` worktree provider only. Under `orca` or `conductor`,
# use `worktrees.seed_files` in raw.config.yml instead — see
# docs/workflow/adapters/worktrees-claude.md.

.env.local
.env.*.local

